From 3627d3971d6491d5ce8b3310295864f2ba96854a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:27:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 185/188] win32u: NEON AlphaBlend, HALFTONE stretching and
 glyph drawing for 32-bit RGB DIBs.

All bit-exact with the C code:
- AlphaBlend (blend_rects_8888): per-pixel alpha and constant alpha blend 8
  pixels at a time, with an exact division by 255. Channels are combined
  with OR as in blend_argb, so a source that isn't premultiplied gives the
  same bits. Constant alpha 255 without source alpha, which
  UpdateLayeredWindow uses, is a copy.
- HALFTONE (halftone_888): the 32-bit fixed-point interpolation runs on all
  four channels with a 32x32->64 multiply, and each source row is
  interpolated across once and kept while the destination rows that use it
  are drawn.
- Glyphs (draw_glyph_8888): aa_color's divisions by 0xff - text and by text
  become multiplies by a reciprocal, exact for these ranges, and the
  per-level ranges a table lookup.

Per 1920x1080 or 1280x800 frame, ms old -> new: HALFTONE 1280x720 to
1920x1080 7.7 -> 2.3; glyphs over the screen 5.8 -> 1.6; per-pixel alpha
0.56 -> 0.41; constant alpha 0.52 -> 0.27; UpdateLayeredWindow's blend 0.07
-> 0.05.
---
 dlls/win32u/dibdrv/primitives.c | 294 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 294 insertions(+)

